> @nizarm can you show us how you would make use of this ?
Hey @normanmaurer  - without this fix - here is how I am using this now

```java
Http2MultiplexHandler multiplexHandler = new Http2MultiplexHandler(unsupportedHandler, unsupportedHandler);  

final HttpClientCodec sourceCodec = new HttpClientCodec(_maxInitialLineLength, _maxHeaderSize, _maxChunkSize);

    UnsupportedHandler unsupportedHandler = new UnsupportedHandler();
   // please note that I am passing a second dummy channel handler as it is mandatory now
   // Once the fix is in place - I will not pass the 2nd argument as that is optional with the fix.
    Http2MultiplexHandler multiplexHandler = new Http2MultiplexHandler(unsupportedHandler, unsupportedHandler);

    Http2ClientUpgradeCodecTemporaryFix upgradeCodec = new Http2ClientUpgradeCodecTemporaryFix(
        (Http2ConnectionHandler) Http2FrameCodecBuilder
        .forClient()
        .initialSettings(createHttp2Settings())
        .build(),
        multiplexHandler
        );

    final ChannelPromise upgradePromise = channel.newPromise();
    channel.attr(NettyChannelAttributes.INITIALIZATION_FUTURE).set(upgradePromise);

    channel.pipeline().addLast(sourceCodec);
    channel.pipeline().addLast(new HttpClientUpgradeHandler(sourceCodec, upgradeCodec, _maxContentLength));

Once the clear text upgrade workflow is completed ... we bootstrap the client side stram channel using bootstrap as follows

final Http2StreamChannelBootstrap bootstrap =
        new Http2StreamChannelBootstrap(channel).handler(new Http2StreamChannelInitializer(_ssl, _maxContentLength));

The Http2StreamChannelInitializer contain all the channel handlers we need for the stream channel.
```

So this fix allows us not to forcefully pass an upgradeStreamHandler as shown in the above comment.

Let me know if you have any questions or concerns on this usage !

//So after the fix we instantiate the multiplex handler as follows (please note - we are now not
//forced to pass the 2nd argument as it is optional now and we are not really using it)
Http2MultiplexHandler multiplexHandler = new Http2MultiplexHandler(unsupportedHandler);

@nizarm hmm... its still not clear to me why this would be a problem tho...

Why you can't just do something like this:

```java
Http2MultiplexHandler multiplexHandler = new Http2MultiplexHandler(..., new ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter() {
    @Override
    public void channelActive(ChannelHandlerContext ctx) throws Exception {
        // This is called once the upgrade was completed
            
        // Obtain the parent channel which is the real connection and bootstrap more http2 streams.
        Http2StreamChannelBootstrap bootstrap = new Http2StreamChannelBootstrap(ctx.channel().parent());
                
        ...
        bootstrap.open().addListener(new FutureListener<Channel>() {
            @Override
            public void operationComplete(Future<Channel> future) throws Exception {
                // Do something with the new stream
            }
        });
    }
});
```
